.TH focusforge-cli-history-delete 1  "delete 0.1.0-rc.3" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-history\-delete \- Delete one checkpoint: it is hidden, and dropped from the project once no visible checkpoint is built on it; its space is reclaimed by `history compact`. Refuses the last visible checkpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli history delete\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\-changed\-sources\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete one checkpoint: it is hidden, and dropped from the project once no visible checkpoint is built on it; its space is reclaimed by `history compact`. Refuses the last visible checkpoint
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR \fI<CHECKPOINT>\fR
The checkpoint to delete \-\- any unique prefix of its id
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the JSON report instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\-changed\-sources\fR
Accept changed source frames, printing their warning instead of refusing
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to delete from
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0\-rc.3
